WEBVTT

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.740
<i>In the prelims,</i>

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:15.820
<i>Iwamine-san finished first</i>

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.440
<i>and I finished second.</i>

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.760
<i>Given the point gap between us and Kurikawa,</i>

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.210
<i>I absolutely have to beat 
her in the semifinals.</i>

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.550
<i>But can I?</i>

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.590
<i>No, don't be negative! I will win!</i>

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.840
<i>I have to live up to the team's 
expectations, or else...</i>

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:47.900
<i>No!</i>

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.360
<i>I don't want to disappoint them!
 I don't want to repeat my past mistakes!</i>

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.360
<i>I've simply </i>got<i> to win!</i>

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.850
<i>I never wanna go through that again!</i>

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.080
<i>I can't let them see me like this.</i>

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.580
<i>Not when I exude so much 
swagger in the public eye.</i>

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:11.430
<i>But, deep down, I'm just a coward who's 
trembling inside whenever she competes.</i>

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:34.610
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.770
<b><i>Wall 6             Unbelievable Ability</i></b>

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.770
Go, go, Konomin!

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.800
Wh-What brought this on, Nono-san?

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.660
You mean my outfit?

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.150
Isn't it obvious?

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.610
I'm your cheerleading squad!

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.820
By the way... I'm sorry, Konomin.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.900
You had to see me cut
 a sorry figure yesterday.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.690
No, you didn't.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:05.410
I may have bombed out, 
but as a member of the Hanamiya team,

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.490
I'll be fighting with you 
out there in spirit.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.320
I want to see you kill it.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.040
Later. I'll be cheering 
you on from the stands.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.730
R-Right...

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:18.030
I'd say she's got 60 percent 
of her energy back,

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.170
though I'm sure she's still 
feeling down about it.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.680
So, it's our job to bring her back up to 100.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.340
Understand?

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.600
Loud and clear.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.920
Go harder, please.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.430
Okay, got it.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:33.100
Hup.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.610
Say, Jun-chan.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.740
St. Caterno's Fujita-san's been 
practicing this whole time.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.060
Shouldn't she ease up a little?

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.030
She'll be fine.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.710
Look at Captain. She's been running nonstop.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.170
I know...

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.790
I wonder what Iwamine-san's listening to.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:52.880
Why don't you go ask her?

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.720
Uh, I'd rather not.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.260
Meanwhile, that girl's studying or something.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.880
Must have college entrance exams.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.880
And what about her?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.510
mwahaha

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.320
Don't ask me.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.510
Must be photosynthesis!

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.220
You can't be serious.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.890
May I have a moment?

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.610
I didn't expect you to be good 
enough to reach the semifinals,

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:12.660
but I suppose that's what a former prima 
at a powerhouse ballet school can do.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.720
I'm not one to talk, given I don't 
have <i>that</i> much climbing experience,

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.150
but you started in high school, right?

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.860
Yeah. It's only been around two months or so.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:23.980
Wha...

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:28.810
Surely I am better than you, then.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:35.170
E-Even if you were a superior ballerina, 
I have the upper hand in climbing, and...

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:39.420
St. Caterno is clearly the stronger team!

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:44.360
Well, you're doing what you can as 
a team with a mere four members.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.810
I remember that tiny girl from yesterday...

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:47.420
Hey!

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.130
We don't have four members.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:52.320
There may be four of us, 
but together we are one.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.060
We're all doing our own thing, 
but none of us are going it alone.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.160
Captain Sayo, Nono-senpai, and Jun-chan...

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.050
When they're there with me,

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:05.070
it gives me an incredible boost of strength.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:11.950
It makes me want to aim higher. 
It makes me want to <i>climb</i> higher.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.240
I know I can go as far as
 I want with the Hanamiya team.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.410
I can scale any wall in my way.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.710
I can't explain it. It's just how I feel.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.460
Is it weird?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:30.470
<i>What? The Kasahara Konomi I knew 
always projected a frailty of sorts.</i>

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.430
<i>But this girl I see now...</i>

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.850
<i>I wasn't wrong to see her as my role model.</i>

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:44.360
Is that so? Well, it'll make 
victory all the sweeter.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.620
What's <i>her</i> problem?

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:51.660
Anyway, you did mention doing ballet before,

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:52.870
but not that you were a prima.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.680
It's not a big deal.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:58.370
It's just kind of been part 
of my life since I was three.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:02.880
Huh? She seemed to be holding 
a grudge over it, though.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.260
Anne-chan!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.040
Cool Kurusu.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.260
Cool Kurusu!

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.460
Nono-chan?

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:14.890
Asu-neesan!

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.900
The Kanto Bouldering Championships 
girls' semifinals are about to begin.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:23.420
I'm joined on commentary 
by routesetter Nakata-san.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.400
Glad to be here.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.360
What brings you here?

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.770
I helped set the routes for the semis.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:31.870
Huh? Really?

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.900
Good to see you again, Juzo-san.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.770
I believe it's our first 
time meeting, Kiku-chan.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:38.500
Huh.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.630
I'm Fujimura Asuka, 
and I run a climbing goods store.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:42.810
Nice to meetcha.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.010
What's the matter?

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:52.510
Oh, nothing. Just that I produced 
works of art for the semifinals, too.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:56.390
I wasn't expecting you to 
be the routesetter for this.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.190
I only helped a little.

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:01.270
Anyway, the level of competition 
has skyrocketed lately.

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:05.100
I knew we were getting better rookies 
by the year, but this is awesome.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:06.020
Sure is.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:10.410
Well, the semis and finals follow 
the conveyor belt system.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.780
Who knows how that will affect the climbers?

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.030
What do you mean, conveyor belt system?

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:18.860
It's called that because the climbers 
appear to be on a conveyor belt.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:20.910
Is that so?

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.830
You get five minutes to attempt the 
first wall, then a five-minute break.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:29.550
Then five minutes for the second, another 
five-minute break, and so on and so forth.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:33.260
Also, it goes in ascending 
order of the prelim standings.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.870
Everyone goes in order, 
attempting the four walls set for them.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:39.810
Unlike a timed session, the climbers
 have to stay in an isolation area.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.820
They aren't allowed to see 
what the others are doing.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.310
In other words,

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.690
it naturally calls for 
acute on-sighting ability.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:52.080
On-sighting requires experience,

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.390
decision-making ability, 
and the physical ability to back that up...

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:57.200
But the most important of all

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:01.330
is the analytic skills needed 
to quickly find the right route.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.330
Th-Then...

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.100
Exactly.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.590
We are ready for the girls' 
semifinals to begin.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:12.090
Up first, we have the promising 
rookie Kasahara Konomi!

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:17.600
<i>Judging from her performance in the prelims, 
these rules should suit her better.</i>

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.350
<i>Nono-san...</i>

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.340
<i>Wish me luck!</i>

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:29.360
She impressed us all by making 
the semifinals as a rookie.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.400
What kind of moves will 
she show us this time?

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:37.620
<i>A flat wall that needs 
balance and coordination.</i>

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:41.110
<i>No inclines puts it right down my alley.</i>

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.870
<i>Picture it...</i>

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.620
<i>Picture yourself climbing</i>

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:48.630
<i>and use that image to solve this problem!</i>

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:02.140
<i>Urk... That crimp two hands up sucks.</i>

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:05.920
<i>But crimping it will limit 
the options for my next move,</i>

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.150
<i>so I'll try to open-hand it.</i>

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:11.000
<i>The crux... has to be the 
lead-up to the zone hold.</i>

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.650
<i>That sequence needs perfect coordination. 
Gotta make sure I don't swing off.</i>

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.410
<i>Good luck, Konomin.</i>

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:28.410
It's easy to tell because I've 
watched her climb from up close.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:30.350
She's got a real knack for this.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:30.990
Yeah.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:34.850
But these walls will be 
difficult for her to send.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:36.170
Why?

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.080
The reason is simple:

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:40.400
their sheer difficulty.

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:44.830
The semifinal routes are meant to 
eliminate all but six finalists,

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:49.440
so they're designed to be just barely 
possible for the top climbers to send.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.800
Looking good, Konomin! You can do this!

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:55.880
Master!

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:58.520
The shoes I picked are doing their job,

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.570
but this is where things get tough.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.450
These problems are in a different league, 
difficulty-wise, than the prelims' were.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.720
I'm sure we'll see a bunch of climbers 
who can't even send one of them.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:10.540
It'll be fine, Asu-neesan. Just you watch.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:19.220
But hasn't it only been a couple of 
months since she picked up climbing?

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:21.720
It's virtually impossible for her to send...

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:36.520
She...

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:37.880
She sends it in one!

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.110
Can you believe it?!

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:44.640
Wh-What's with these loud cheers?

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.370
No way...

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:48.370
Sounds like Konomi-san sent it.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:52.500
Did she do it?

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:55.130
Yes!

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:57.050
H-How?

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:01.560
That's just our Konomin, Asu-neesan.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:05.520
<i>On-sighting the very first problem 
in the semis that easily?</i>

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.890
<i>You truly are special, Kasahara Konomi!</i>

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:12.150
<i>She can't be judged as a 
mere rookie at this point.</i>

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:15.590
<i>We're witnessing the birth 
of climbing's new star...</i>

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:18.150
<i>Or should I say, invader?</i>

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.180
Cool, Kurusu.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:28.500
Kasahara Konomi from Hanamiya Girls', eh?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.640
She's a cool Kurusutomer, isn't she?

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:34.000
Y-Yeah.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.500
These cheers... It was probably a one-shot.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:41.280
If the 20th-ranked Kasahara-san one-shot it,

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:43.760
we can't afford to fail Problem A, we can't.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:47.450
Jun.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:48.920
She did it.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.870
We have to do our best to keep up.

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.270
Our next climber is Satou 
Maruno from Kurikawa High.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:12:00.280
<i>But flip that around, and the 
fact that she one-shot it</i>

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:03.710
<i>means it can't have been all that difficult.</i>

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.030
<i>I'll one-shot it too, I will!</i>

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:11.070
<i>This crimp is pretty hard to grasp.</i>

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:14.290
<i>And this third hold is easy 
to swing off, it is.</i>

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:16.290
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:20.040
<i>So, this is a semifinal problem...</i>

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:22.920
<i>It's several levels above 
the prelims, it is!</i>

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.640
I'm not done yet.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.790
Oh, dear!

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:32.430
Satou has yet to even secure the zone,

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:35.060
but her time is up!

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:39.320
<i>M-Miss Kashahara shent </i>this<i> thing in one?!</i>

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:43.520
Now that's more like it. That's 
how it's normally supposed to go!

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.950
Yeah, well, Konomin isn't normal.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:49.680
Next up, we have Kasahara 
attempting Problem B.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.240
Over at Problem A,

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:54.000
we have Matsuhashi High's Niijima.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.100
Always be a challenger.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:59.980
This competition is her first 
time clearing the prelims.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.630
She used several attempts in the prelims.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:06.300
What does she have in store for us?

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.240
Whoa, and that ends her first try already.

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:19.610
<i>Wow, the very second hand is tough.</i>

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:22.010
<i>But where there's a will, there's a way.</i>

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:28.620
Again!

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:34.500
I'm not done.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.600
She's already on her fourth attempt.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.370
That's gotta be rough.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:40.000
Yeah.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:44.010
But she's getting higher with every attempt.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.260
Hell...

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:49.390
This time!

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:52.640
She's absurdly quick to pick 
herself up and try again.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.840
<i>Niijima-senpai is usually slow and clumsy,</i>

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:00.740
<i>but she recovers abnormally quickly.</i>

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.760
<i>It's why she can make a 
high number of attempts.</i>

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:05.210
I won't give up.

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.530
<i>With each attempt,</i>

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.280
<i>she gets higher and higher...</i>

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:15.000
<i>until she reaches the top!</i>

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.600
Where there's a will, there's a way.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:20.000
Dreams do come true.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.340
<i>The way she climbs, falls, and climbs again</i>

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:29.100
<i>makes her look like a zombie! 
Even death can't keep her down!</i>

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:30.890
<i>That's Zombie Niijima!</i>

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:34.720
I'm on her team, and even 
I can barely handle this.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:35.640
But...

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.570
Never give up.

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:43.020
It's not over until it's over.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:47.870
<i>She doesn't fare well in prelims cause she 
can't immediately retry after a fall,</i>

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.150
<i>but she might have a real 
chance in these semis!</i>

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.160
Did she do it?

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.590
I-Incredible!

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:59.410
I... I can't believe my eyes.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:02.290
Dreams... huh?

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.790
What the fur are you 
doing all the way there?!

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:07.630
Kasahara Konomi sends it in one again!

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:09.800
What is her deal?!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.020
Again?

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:12.680
That's some wild cheering.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:15.980
<i>I think it's Matsuhashi High's 
Niijima Kaoru right now.</i>

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:19.520
<i>Her, and... Kasahara Konomi on Problem B.</i>

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.730
<b>Isolation 
Area 1</b>

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.860
That volume two hands up...

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.300
I should push into it a little...

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:29.560
Konomi?

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:32.070
And then for the edge foothold...

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:32.070
Hey, you okay?

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.740
Oh, Jun-chan. What's up?

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:36.900
Uh, well...

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.600
Are you tired?

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.460
Nah, not at all.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.790
That's good.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:44.130
You should still relax your body.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:48.630
I know, don't worry! I feel like 
I can keep climbing forever today!

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:52.920
Uh... Look, just rest up 
for these five minutes.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.550
At least wipe your sweat off.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.400
Oh, right.

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:58.060
I forgot I wanted to do that.

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:03.810
Next, Hanamiya's Kasahara 
Konomi attempts Problem C,

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:07.070
Matsuhashi's Niijima 
Kaoru attempts Problem B,

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:11.050
and at Problem A, we have 
St. Caterno's Ooba Kurea.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:13.380
<i>Kasahara Konomi...</i>

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:42.100
<i>Picture it.</i>

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:44.840
<i>Picture yourself solving this problem.</i>

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:54.370
<i>Installation is finished.</i>

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.070
<i>Ready. Game start.</i>

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:00.220
Attempting Problem A now is Prelims Rank 16,

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.500
ex-ballet dancer Ooba Kurea.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:06.330
<i>Those cheers rang out pretty 
quickly for Problem A.</i>

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:07.960
<i>Which means...</i>

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:11.120
<i>Kasahara-san one-shot it.</i>

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:15.240
<i>And when the second wave came, 
Kasahara-san was on Problem B.</i>

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:19.500
<i>Niijima-san couldn't have 
sent Problem A in one.</i>

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:20.510
<i>More likely...</i>

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.770
<i>Another Kasahara one-shot.</i>

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:30.580
<i>I can't be outdone, then. I must send 
this in one with poise and grace.</i>

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:33.030
Dreams come true!

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:38.030
<i>This crimp has a pretty flimsy grip.</i>

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.910
<i>The footholds are no better.</i>

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:44.540
<i>That said, my exquisite sense of 
balance will make this easy...</i>

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:48.670
<i>Huh? Why is that hold angled that way?</i>

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:49.790
<i>Do I have to jump?</i>

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.880
<i>When I'm practically stuck to the wall?</i>

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:54.860
<i>Only when climbing do I actually realize</i>

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:58.550
<i>how hard the next hold is to really secure.</i>

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:02.010
<i>And she one-shot it? No...</i>

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.270
<i>How is that possible?</i>

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.700
Ooba falls!

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.950
<i>Oh, for the love of... 
There goes the one-shot.</i>

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:14.440
<i>I have to bounce back from this, 
no matter what!</i>

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:19.270
Did Ooba slip just now? How unlike her.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:25.450
<i>An overhang with an incline 
almost as steep as a roof...</i>

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:29.710
<i>This type of wall is my worst nightmare, 
because it needs so much physical strength.</i>

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:34.400
<i>Do I put both feet on the volume 
and do a sit start of sorts?</i>

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:35.630
<i>No, that's not right.</i>

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:39.310
<i>If I do that, it'll put the 
third pocket just out of reach.</i>

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:44.220
<i>Instead, I should deadpoint the nearby 
pocket and turn away from the volume.</i>

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:46.440
Okay, next hold...

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:50.250
The others are already on their 
second and third attempts,

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:53.470
but Kasahara remains rooted to the spot.

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:56.480
We saw this when she attempted 
Problems A and B, too.

00:18:56.930 --> 00:19:00.240
Her style is to take her time analyzing 
the route before sending it in one.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.620
She climbs in a completely different 
manner to the other competitors.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:09.440
I knew Master's analytic skills 
were good, but not <i>this</i> good.

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:11.900
Uh... is she mumbling to herself?

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:13.050
Oh, man.

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:16.590
That gave me a start the 
first time I saw it, too.

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:18.410
But you know what?

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:21.380
Konomin is super good when she 
gets in the zone like this!

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:30.060
<i>And to finish it off, it's crucial 
to do a toe hook with my right foot.</i>

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.900
<i>That'll let me reach the 
top hold with my left hand.</i>

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:34.540
<i>Okay, I solved it.</i>

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:38.120
<i>Now I just have to trace 
that solution with my body.</i>

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:41.530
Kasahara finally makes her move. 
Will she be able to climb as she envisioned?

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:44.720
The observation process is only mental,
at the end of the day.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:46.780
The actual climb is a whole 
different can of worms.

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:51.160
If you have time, making several 
attempts like the others are doing

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.430
and familiarizing your body with 
the route is the better option.

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:57.230
But Master's one-shot both problems so far.

00:19:57.230 --> 00:20:00.050
She's climbing like she's made 
countless attempts already.

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:02.240
That's what makes it so impressive.

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:05.050
She solves the problems in her 
mind with insane precision.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:09.620
<i>I was desperate to do well in 
these semis after making it here,</i>

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:13.700
<i>but that doesn't matter right now!</i>

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:15.440
<i>I'm having so much fun!</i>

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:19.690
<i>Unlike the prelims, you can't glean 
any information from other climbers.</i>

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:23.700
<i>And I had no idea solving problems 
with no beta was this fun.</i>

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:27.720
<i>I mean, in my eyes, these on-sighting walls</i>

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:31.560
<i>are like brand-new puzzles 
designed just for me!</i>

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.120
<i>And if they're puzzles, I gotta solve them.</i>

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:43.720
<i>I gotta clear them all the way!</i>

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:50.320
<i>No way.</i>

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:53.310
<i>She one-shot three routes in a row?</i>

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:02.900
<i>This is it. I must send it this time.</i>

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:05.910
<i>If I keep falling, I'll...</i>

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:10.860
Why?

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:15.290
Why can you climb these walls, but not I?

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:18.540
I refuse to accept this sacrilege!

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.620
Eek!

00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:35.060
And that's time up!

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:38.060
Ooba couldn't finish solving the problem!

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:43.440
What is going <i>on?</i>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b><i>Wall 7: Failure of a Climber</i></b>
